OL,3,CBurnham says he will stand up to Trump
OL,4,C'if right for Britain'
OL,6,FAndy Burnham says he will publicly
OL,7,Fdisagree with Donald Trump, if it
OL,8,Fmeant defending Britain's interests
OL,9,F"before anything else".
OL,11,FThe new Prime Minister and US
OL,12,FPresident spoke over the phone on
OL,13,FMonday, within an hour of Burnham
OL,14,Farriving in Downing Street.
OL,16,F"I can't at any point say that I won't
OL,17,Ftake a different opinion from him
OL,18,F(Donald Trump), that I will need to
OL,19,Fvoice a different idea that is right
OL,20,Ffor Britain.
OL,26,@qD@AOUqD@VO]xD@AOUzD@ApmzD@Npn
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,308,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30702
SC,0002
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F307A1785071911
OL,3,CBurnham says he will stand up to Trump
OL,4,C'if right for Britain'
OL,6,F"You have to defend your own national
OL,7,Finterest before anything else. That's
OL,8,Fwhat you're required to do if you're
OL,9,Fto do this job properly," he told the
OL,10,FBBC's Sunday with Laura Kuenssberg
OL,11,Fprogramme.
OL,13,FAfter the call, Trump stated in a post
OL,14,Fon Truth Social that Burnham "has got
OL,15,Fa big job ahead of him, but he will be
OL,16,Fable to do it" and pledged that the US
OL,17,F"will be there to help".
OL,19,FDowning Street described the 20-minute
OL,20,Fconversation as "extremely warm".
