OL,3,CBurnham says he will stand up to Trump
OL,4,C'if right for Britain'
OL,6,FIt comes after relations between
OL,7,FWashington and Sir Keir Starmer's
OL,8,Fgovernment became increasingly
OL,9,Ffractious over the Iran conflict.
OL,11,FBurnham also ruled out an early
OL,12,Fgeneral election in his first major
OL,13,Finterview, saying Britain had "voted
OL,14,Ffor a manifesto" in 2024.
OL,16,F"There's no early general election. I
OL,17,Fdon't think people want it," he said.
OL,26,@uD@_OUvD@PO]xD@AOUyD@\O]
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/7
OL,2,W/*%+,"-/.!,.!T,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,23,TppppppppppppppppppGsource: itv.com/news
OL,24,ANext Page BNat News CNat TV FClean Feed
FL,308,300,200,140,000,100
PN,30704
SC,0004
CT,2,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F307A1785071911
OL,3,CBurnham says he will stand up to Trump
OL,4,C'if right for Britain'
OL,6,FHe added: "I just think what I most
OL,7,Fneed to do is get Britain focused on
OL,8,Fgetting the country back where it
OL,9,Fshould be."
OL,11,FSubscribe for free to our weekly
OL,12,Fnewsletter for exclusive and original
OL,13,Fcoverage from ITV News. Direct to your
OL,14,Finbox every Friday morning.
OL,16,FDefence policy remained a key issue
OL,17,Fduring the interview, with the PM also
OL,18,Frefusing to be drawn on a timetable
OL,19,Ffor increasing spending to three per
OL,20,Fcent of GDP.
OL,26,@nD@KOUqD@KO]
